IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp5-months`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division D (Payment of Benefits: Special Rules Applicable)
-- POST-RETIREMENT BENEFIT: sections 76.1 (when it is payable) and 76.2 (how long it is paid).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- A month is the DATE of its first day. The basic exemption (section 20, piece cp1) and the month the contributory
-- period ends (subparagraph 49(b)(iii), piece cp3: the month before the retirement pension commences) are taken
-- as plain inputs.

-- out of range: section 20 (piece cp1): the basic exemption, a plain input `the contributor's basic exemption`
-- out of range: subparagraph 49(b)(iii) (piece cp3): the end of the contributory period, taken as `first month for which the retirement pension is payable`
-- out of range: sections 5 to 20 (pieces cp1 and cp2): that a contribution was made in respect of the earnings, a plain input

§ `Part II, Division D -- Post-retirement benefit (sections 76.1 and 76.2)`

§§ `Section 76.1 -- when a post-retirement benefit is payable`

-- src:2410 | 76.1 Subject to section 62, a post-retirement benefit is payable to a beneficiary of a retirement pension for each month commencing with January 1 of the year following the year of a contributor’s earnings if
-- src:2411 | (a) a contribution has been made in respect of those earnings;
-- src:2412 | (b) those earnings exceed the contributor’s basic exemption; and
-- src:2413 | (c) those earnings are for a period that
-- src:2414 | (i) begins after 2011 and after the contributory period ends under subparagraph 49(b)(iii), and
-- src:2415 | (ii) ends with the month preceding the month in which the contributor reaches seventy years of age.
@ref Act s 76.1 "begins after 2011" (src:2414)
`s 76.1(c)(i) — the day after which the period of the earnings must begin` MEANS YearMonthDay 2011 12 31

@ref Act s 76.1 (src:2410-2415)
GIVEN `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contribution has been made in respect of the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `first day of the period of the earnings` IS A DATE
      `last day of the period of the earnings` IS A DATE
      `first month for which the retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE
      `date of birth of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `year of the earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76.1 — the first month for which a post-retirement benefit is payable` `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension` `a contribution has been made in respect of the earnings` `the earnings` `the contributor's basic exemption` `first day of the period of the earnings` `last day of the period of the earnings` `first month for which the retirement pension is payable` `date of birth of the contributor` `year of the earnings` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension`
       -- (a) a contribution has been made in respect of those earnings
       AND `a contribution has been made in respect of the earnings`
       -- (b) those earnings exceed the contributor's basic exemption
       AND `the earnings` ABOVE `the contributor's basic exemption`
       -- (c)(i) the period begins after 2011 and after the contributory period ends under subparagraph 49(b)(iii)
       --        (the month before the month the retirement pension commences)
       AND `first day of the period of the earnings` ABOVE `s 76.1(c)(i) — the day after which the period of the earnings must begin`
       AND `first day of the period of the earnings` AT LEAST `first month for which the retirement pension is payable`
       -- (c)(ii) the period ends with the month preceding the month in which the contributor reaches 70
       --         (read as: ends no later than that month; NOTES.md, fork F12)
       AND `last day of the period of the earnings` BELOW `cp5 helper -- the month in which the person reaches an age under section 2(2)` `date of birth of the contributor` 70
    -- each month commencing with January 1 of the year following the year of the earnings
    THEN JUST (YearMonthDay (`year of the earnings` PLUS 1) 1 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 76.2 -- how long a post-retirement benefit is paid`

-- src:2416 | Duration of payment
-- src:2417 | 76.2 Subject to this Act, a post-retirement benefit shall continue to be paid during the lifetime of the beneficiary and shall cease with the payment for the month in which the beneficiary dies.
@ref Act s 76.2 (src:2417)
GIVEN `day the beneficiary died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76.2 — the last month for which a post-retirement benefit is paid` `day the beneficiary died` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `day the beneficiary died`
